00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:20.780
<v Ira  Glass>Penn State's administration does a pretty thorough job surveying students to track how much they're drinking. The surveys show that every Friday and every Saturday night, 75% of the school drinks. That's over 30,000 people, an average of four and a half drinks per person. And the students drink those drinks in about three hours average.
<v Ira  Glass>宾州立大学的管理层非常彻底地调查学生，追踪他们的饮酒量。调查显示，每个周五和周六晚上，75%的学校在喝酒。那是超过3万人，每人平均喝四杯半。而学生们平均在三个小时内喝掉这些酒。

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:34.370
<v Ira  Glass>To put those numbers in perspective, binge drinking, or as it's being re-branded lately, high risk or dangerous drinking, defined as four drinks for a woman or five drinks for a man consumed in just two hours.
<v Ira  Glass>为了从角度理解这些数字，酗酒，或者最近被重新定义为高风险或危险饮酒，被定义为女性喝四杯或男性喝五杯，仅在两小时内消费完。

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.300
<v Ira  Glass>[SINGING]
<v Ira  Glass>[唱歌]

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:51.440
<v Ira  Glass>When you get down into the details of Penn State's numbers, it works out to over half the students regularly binge drinking, which is just a little bit above the national average for college students.
<v Ira  Glass>当你深入了解宾州立大学的具体数字时，算出超过一半的学生经常酗酒，这仅仅比全国大学生的平均水平高出一点点。

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:54.400
<v Ira  Glass>[SINGING]
<v Ira  Glass>[唱歌]

00:15:54.400 --> 00:16:10.750
<v Ira  Glass>The routine at Penn State on weekend nights is that you pregame or preload. That's what they call it when you drink at your apartment or your dorm room before going out. It's way cheaper than buying drinks at a bar. Also in winter, keeps you warm. We heard lots of people use the phrase "beer jacket."
<v Ira  Glass>宾州立大学周末晚上的惯例是预热或载入。这就是他们所说的在出门前在公寓或宿舍喝酒。这比在酒吧买酒便宜得多。而且在冬天，还能保暖。我们听很多人用“啤酒外套”这个词。

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:22.310
<v Ira  Glass>And if you went to college long ago, you definitely noticed mostly hard liquor here, not beer. Various sugary vodka drinks of various kinds. Red bull and vodka, one of them. So everybody gets a lot more drunk.
<v Ira  Glass>如果你很久以前上过大学，你肯定注意到这里主要是烈酒，不是啤酒。各种各样的含糖伏特加饮料。红牛加伏特加是其中一种。所以每个人都喝得更醉。

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.920
<v Female Student 4>To living single, to seeing double.
<v Female Student 4>为了单身生活，为了看东西重影。

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.610
<v Female Student 5>Oh. And what's the triple?
<v Female Student 5>噢。那三倍是什么？

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:39.210
<v Jane Feltes>Early on one night, I went to an apartment with a bunch of seniors. And they were getting ready and pregaming. They said they usually do five shots in five minutes before they leave the house. There were empties everywhere.
